    "[taal, protected word] 'Om dit verder te neem is die werk van grootmense soos': 'dit verder neem' is a calque of English 'take it further'; idiomatic Afrikaans would be e.g. 'die saak verder te voer' or 'verder daarmee te gaan', if the writer wishes to reconsider.",
    "[taal, protected word] 'Dan kan hulle 'n maatskaplike werker of die polisie inbring': 'inbring' calques English 'bring in'; 'betrek' is the idiomatic Afrikaans verb here, while keeping 'kan'.",
    "[taal, protected word] 'As dit veilig is, mag jy 'Nee' sê en weggaan, ook vir 'n gro': This sentence writes 'Nee' quoted and capitalised, while the protected sentence two lines later writes 'nee sê' in lower case; the two forms should probably match."
